{
  "_meta": {
    "description": "Interruption card definitions for the Warlock Table. Category = 'interruption' covers all tarot cards, split into four subtypes: boon, person, aura, random_table. Scene cards (the 5 MTG mana cards) are defined separately and are NOT included in this file.",
    "subtype_rules": {
      "boon": "One-time announcement cue. Meaning is narrative/GM-declared, not mechanical. All four share the same light pattern (boon_comet_flash) and same placeholder audio clip; only suit_color differs.",
      "person": "One-time announcement cue (flash + clip), then the table returns to whatever it was doing. Not persistent. Each card has a distinct built-in light signature (color + pattern). 'npc_binding' is null by default — the GM fills this in per-campaign via the card management UI without touching the light/audio definition.",
      "aura": "Timed flourish. Layers on top of whatever scene/pattern is currently running for duration_seconds, then fades back to the base scene automatically. Not persistent past its duration.",
      "random_table": "Does not resolve to its own effect directly. Instead picks a card from a target pool (here: all 12 aura cards) via the given selection method, then fires that card's effect as if it had been tapped directly. Wheel of Fortune uses uniform_random with repeats allowed — no repeat-avoidance or weighting."
    },
    "default_aura_duration_seconds": 60
  },
